  "description": "LUYYUB crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C76 H80 Cl4 Dy8 N28 O16,2(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 3 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 3 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 3 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 3 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.732-3.879 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 101.18-110.76°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C76H80Cl4Dy8N28O16·2(CH4O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Dy(III).",
